This peer completes the effective back-and-forth construction between the computable presentations of Scott's universal domains \(U\) and \(V\).

<!-- formalization -->

**Definition (`effectiveIso812_UV`).** The computable presentations of \(U\) and \(V\) are effectively isomorphic.

*Proof.* The effective back-and-forth theorem applies because both presentations have computable difference and union operations, positive and difference-closed neighbourhood structures, no minimal non-master neighbourhoods, computable splitting operations, nonempty master neighbourhoods, and compatible distinguished initial elements. ∎
